       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg/day is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg. I don't know of any condition or stage of treatment where that dose is indicated, and higher doses raise the risk of serotonin toxicity, seizures, and arrhythmia without adding benefit.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter up to 200 mg by mouth once daily right now. If you want to titrate toward that, I can enter a lower dose.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, a psychiatry or clinical pharmacy consult can confirm it. Once the order has been reviewed and approved through your hospital's process, I can help enter it.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 1000 mg was a slip for 100 mg, I'll enter 100 mg as soon as you say so.\n\nWhich would you like?"
